From 09cb7f1f649d5f2325f45d07e87b32ca6537df34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ccr <ccr@aciceri.dev>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:15:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] collab: carry live voice audio between host and a guest

A live call could only run on the machine holding the audio devices, so a
collab guest could read and steer a session but never talk to it.

Add four additive frames: live-ctl and live-audio guest-to-host, live-state
and live-out host-to-guest. COLLAB_PROTO stays 3 because both sides already
ignore unknown frame types, so a stock guest or host is unaffected.

CollabHost routes them through a CollabLiveAudioBridge that the interactive
/live controller registers, keeping collab free of live internals and the
live controller free of collab internals. One peer owns live audio at a
time; ownership is released when that peer leaves.

Output frames whose peak is silence are dropped. The remote track runs for
the whole call and is almost entirely silence, so relaying it verbatim cost
2.9 MB where a gated stream costs 51 KB for the same reply.

(cherry picked from commit 8f3786f27a38c3600d3b820ccabd4c14f0740fab)
